{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779639797,"nonce":"Y493sX6ZeneeaDiaZznRvAr2HJM=","message":"## Subsuming `a3e46d5`: remaining material copied forward\n\nThis audit umbrella now supersedes `a3e46d5` (`Umbrella: Studio product-depth and Feedbax contract sequence`). The issue-ID coverage from `a3e46d5` is accounted for here; the IDs that were not already named in this audit were closed foundation issues or commit/comment hashes, not untracked open implementation work:\n\n- closed foundation/spec issues: `5378a5d`, `c07eae1`, `57c18dd`, `0fcb25a`, `c6b1b73`, `e08aeb5`, `4178e12`;\n- related merge/commit evidence: `00867ff`, `3957292`, `7baf3cc`, `a907bff`, `e5dd86b`, `4ac5106`, `0398cff`, `7cfe6a9`, `27384a2`, `2f2f6b6`;\n- RLRMP artifact hashes from `5c6b294`: `f47abb1`, `3702f54`, `b399efc`.\n\nThe unique useful material from `a3e46d5` is implementation guidance and prior-progress context, not additional open issues. Preserve these points when using this umbrella:\n\n### Merged foundation context\n\nAlready-landed foundations include provider/manifest MVP and deterministic execution contract from the closed `fa3978f` roadmap path; Scenario Projection Workspace foundations from closed `5378a5d`; the schema contract overhaul from closed `c07eae1`; task-binding hardening from closed `57c18dd`; authoring/runtime graph normalization from closed `0fcb25a`; and the first bounded delayed-reach task-panel timeline slice under `bd5aefb`.\n\nRecent progress that should not be redone:\n\n- `e08aeb5` / commit `3957292` / merge `00867ff`: fixed graph training target selectors and the wrong-object training risk for that path.\n- `4178e12` / commit `a907bff` / merge `7baf3cc`: lowered worker graph task bindings for the current supported Studio graph path. It does not finish every graph-as-model lowering case, but it removes the old assumption that no lowering substrate exists.\n- `bd5aefb` commits `4ac5106`, `0398cff`, `7cfe6a9` / merge `e5dd86b`: delivered a bounded delayed-reach task timeline/editor surface and graph-authoring boundary cleanup. This is scaffolding, not the final shared ValueSpec/function/distribution editor.\n- `0258fac` / commit `2f2f6b6` / merge `27384a2`: delivered a substantial schema/dimension/recurrence UX slice, including Task Data sample-view dimensions, mux concat inference, Network/mechanics dimension sync, compatibility/invalid-draft feedback, explicit `instant | recurrent` wire temporality, recurrent initializer metadata, same-step instant-cycle validation, default recurrent edges for new cycle-closing edges, dashed `t+1` rendering, recurrent edge properties, and GRU/LSTM hidden recurrence as explicit recurrent edges in opened Network internals.\n\n### Workspace authoring requirements\n\nWorkspace work is not just UI polish. `946c859` and `6a094c9` should preserve the `a3e46d5` direction: Workspace must become a faithful task/mechanics/objective authoring surface over `StudioScenarioSpec`, not a decorative projection or passive status view. It should support selecting task objects, goals, effectors, mechanics entities, and objective overlays; creating objectives/losses/metrics from related entities such as effector plus goal state error; showing inherited vs overridden train/eval state; validating source-target compatibility through typed selector/value metadata; and writing to objective/task/mechanics specs rather than hidden React state.\n\nStart bounded: 2D reaching/task mechanics and objective creation first, not a general CAD/3D editor.\n\n### Preemption rule\n\nThe sequence in this audit is the product/architecture order, not permission to ignore correctness blockers. If active work hits a live correctness blocker, fix or split that first. Examples: wrong-object training risks like `e08aeb5`, checkpoint collisions `ae2d692`, static JAX metadata recompilation `96a0725` / `29c89d8`, and worker lowering failures on supported topologies.\n\n### Mandible boundary\n\nFeedbax owns provider schemas, validation, registries, execution semantics, Studio entry points, manifests, and local artifact refs. Mandible owns provider registry, graph/provenance ingestion, artifact storage policy, reviewed actions, issue/session/auth graph, and agent workflow surfaces. Feedbax should remain standalone; Mandible should enrich and orchestrate through provider capabilities. Do not put Mandible-specific assumptions into Feedbax schemas.\n\n### Done criteria inherited from `a3e46d5`\n\nThis audit umbrella can close only when concrete child issues exist for each active slice; Workspace can author real task/mechanics/objective relationships over scenario state; shared value/function/distribution editing is used by task timelines and at least one non-task surface; port/selector/value compatibility is visible and explainable; probes/metrics/interventions have a coherent runtime/product story; worker lowering consumes graph/spec/task-binding contracts for the supported execution path; and provider/manifests expose enough evaluation/analysis/report/artifact depth for Mandible and standalone Studio to share durable records.\n\nWith these details copied forward, `a3e46d5` can be closed as subsumed by this umbrella.","files":null}]}